* What's New in GNU Hyperbole by Bob Weiner

`========================================================================='


1 V9.3.2
════════

  `========================================================================='


1.1 DOCUMENTATION
─────────────────

  *** : HY-NEWS has been renamed to HY-NEWS.org.

  When an Org link with an embedded button is activated with {C-c C-o}
  and Hyperbole has not yet been loaded but is installed, it will
  autoload Hyperbole to run the action for the button.

  *** : Add missing entries from the current HyWiki menu.


  `========================================================================='


2 V9.3.1
════════

  `========================================================================='


2.1 ACTION TYPES  (See ).
─────────────────────────

  *** : Improve documentation and variable naming in this actype that
      activates a series of local or global Hyperbole buttons by name.


2.2 DOCUMENTATION
─────────────────

  *** : Add a link to .  and add two recent article and video links:
      [HyRolo: Records are Trees, Not Lines] [Implicit Buttons: Build
      Your Hyperverse]

  *** : Reprioritize single line region and link to Koutline kcell as
      the first two highest priority types in the table.

  *** and : Add {C-c ; h} into the key binding table.  Also, change C-0
      to M-0 and C–1 to M–1 since control digits don't typically work on
      a terminal.

  *** and : Move {C-c C-]} to {C-c [}.

  *** and : Move {C-c ; b} to {C-c ]}.

  *** : Move {C-c C-c} to {C-c ; b} to match with {C-c ; c} binding.

  *** : In (defil search-git-log), change to use curly braces instead of
      square brackets so it can be embedded within Org links.

  *** : Add a commented out setting that shows all of the note taking
      systems that can be quickly full-text searched with HyRolo with no
      indexing.

  *** : Add description of the use and setting of this custom option.

  *** : Add optional setting that enables highlighting Hyperbole buttons
      as Org links when wrapped in double square brackets.


[HyRolo: Records are Trees, Not Lines] <https://youtu.be/5Oo_KqVcLFM>

[Implicit Buttons: Build Your Hyperverse] <https://youtu.be/o2KMvSCXwlU>


2.3 HYROLO  (See ).
───────────────────

  *** Optimize by filtering files to search with ripgrep/grep to only
      those with at least one match.


2.4 IMPLICIT BUTTONS  (See ).
─────────────────────────────

  *** : Add support for Org/MediaWiki links around curly brace-delimited
      key series, e.g.. .

  *** : Allow for Org link square bracket delimiters so can match within
      an call.

  *** `search-git-log': Change to use curly braces instead of square
      brackets so it can be embedded within Org links.


2.5 KOUTLINER  (See ).
──────────────────────

  *** INCOMPATIBLE CHANGE: Move {C-c C-]} to {C-c [} for toggling the
      mode of the {TAB} key, as is easier-to-type and is a 'left'
      opening brace like left 'TAB' key.

    *** INCOMPATIBLE CHANGE: Move {C-c ; b} to {C-c ]}.  Move {C-c C-c}
        to {C-c ; b} to match with {C-c ; c} binding.  {C-c C-c} no
        longer worked because Org-compatibility overrode its binding.  …
        …
